Version 1.41.2 — 2026-11-24
Previous GitHub release: v1.41.1 (2026-11-23)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.41.2 closes the review findings: a failed layer or database read is now
visible as a problem instead of a silent "no problems", field types work on
QGIS 4 / Qt 6, the DBF name limits apply to shapefiles only, and the project
got CI, an MIT license and a clean repository.

Changes in 1.41.2
-----------------
- A layer that cannot be read is reported as "Проверка не выполнена для слоя …"
  in the issues column and in the log instead of disappearing from the
  statistics; this covers every attribute check, the duplicates check and the
  GeoPackage table/column queries.
- Field types are compared through QMetaType.Type with a QVariant fallback, so
  the attribute checks work on QGIS 4 / Qt 6 where QVariant.String is gone.
- The DBF field name limits (10 characters, Latin characters, spaces, invalid
  characters, truncation duplicates) apply to shapefiles only; GeoPackage,
  GeoJSON and other formats are no longer flagged.
- The duplicates check describes its 50 000 feature limit and explains that
  cancellation works between files.
- Added GitHub Actions: lint and unit tests on push and pull requests, tests,
  build and release from a tag.
- LICENSE is the canonical MIT text, the duplicate LICENSE.md is removed, and
  release archives are no longer committed to the repository.
- Removed a duplicate i18n import and completed the English translations.
- Shortened the plugin description and about text in metadata.txt and fixed
  the attribute_check module docstring.
ZGeo change log
===============
Version 1.41.1 — 2026-11-23
Previous GitHub release: v1.41.0 (2026-11-22)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.41.1 turns the check report into a working tool: a right click on a
results cell loads the layers into the project and shows only the problem
features, problem cells are highlighted in pink, and the toolbar survives QGIS
restarts. Also fixes the topology spatial index deprecation and the date check
for QDate values.

Changes in 1.41.1
-----------------
- A right click on a results table cell offers "Load into the current project
  and show on the map": the layer is opened or added, only the features of
  that cell are selected, the map zooms to their extent and the attribute
  table opens; file findings open the folder or the .prj file instead.
- "Load into the current project and show on the map" adds the layer to the map
  canvas layer set, not only to the project tree, so the features are actually
  visible; the extent is transformed into the canvas CRS and a missing
  zoomToFeatureIds falls back to setExtent.
- Fixed a crash in the file navigation: Path.name was called as a method.
- "Load into the current project and show on the map" no longer opens Explorer:
  findings without features are skipped and counted in the status bar, and only
  a .prj finding opens the .prj file itself.
- The topology check uses QgsSpatialIndex.addFeature instead of the deprecated
  insertFeature, so QGIS 3.40+ no longer logs a DeprecationWarning.
- "Load into the current project and show on the map" now works for checks that
  report per field: the finding carries the ids of the affected features, so the
  layer is added, only those features are selected, the map zooms to them and
  the attribute table opens; the date check reads QDate/QDateTime values.
- The toolbar no longer disappears after QGIS is restarted: a restored toolbar
  is reused instead of being deleted, hiding on shutdown is not saved, and the
  user choice is stored in QgsSettings and applied on the next start.
- The ZGeo toolbar is restored when QGIS hides it after startup or after a
  project is opened: visibility is checked on several timers and on the
  initializationCompleted and projectRead signals.
- Results table cells with findings are highlighted in pink, with a legend next
  to the table title.
- The detailed issue dialog also has that button and the same context menu on
  a single finding.

Version 1.41.0 — 2026-11-22
Previous GitHub release: v1.40.0 (2026-11-21)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.41.0 adds three attribute data checks and two spatial checks: text
encoding (mojibake), mixed types in a field, empty fields, extension and
content mismatch, and duplicates by attributes and geometry; 32 checks in
total.

Changes in 1.41.0
-----------------
- Added a "Text encoding (mojibake)" check: text values that look like UTF-8
  read with a single-byte encoding, such as "ÐœÐ¾ÑÐºÐ²Ð°" instead of "Москва",
  reported per field with feature counts, shares, a sample and the repaired
  text when it can be restored.
- Added a "Mixed types in a field" check: text columns where numbers and text
  appear in the same field, which makes Excel and SQL infer the column type
  differently and breaks sorting, sums and filters, reported per field with
  numeric/text counts, shares and examples.
- Added an "Empty fields (100% NULL)" check: columns whose values are all NULL
  or empty strings, which have nothing to export, take up space in the schema
  and can break data exchange, reported per layer and field.
- Added an "Extension and content mismatch" check: files whose content does not
  match the extension, detected by magic signatures (SQLite, Shapefile, ZIP,
  TIFF, JPEG 2000, NetCDF, HDF, Parquet, Arrow, FlatGeobuf, PMTiles, OLE2,
  JSON, XML), reported with the detected content kind.
- Added an "Attribute and geometry duplicates" check: features where both all
  attribute values and the WKB geometry match, reported per layer with matching
  pairs, duplicate and group counts; the geometry-only and attributes-only
  checks stay as they are.
- The results table counts duplicate findings per pair instead of counting the
  summary line, so the number matches the detailed list.

Unreleased
----------
- A right click on a results table cell offers "Load into the current project
  and show on the map": the layer is opened or added, only the features of
  that cell are selected, the map zooms to their extent and the attribute
  table opens; file findings open the folder or the .prj file instead.
- The detailed issue dialog also has that button and the same context menu on
  a single finding.
Version 1.40.0 — 2026-11-21
Previous GitHub release: v1.39.0 (2026-11-19)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.40.0 moves the checks to two quality tabs, adds a results table with
per-file statistics and a detailed issue dialog, an "Add to current project"
button, and eleven new attribute data checks (27 checks total).

Changes in 1.40.0
-----------------
- Added a case-insensitive duplicate field name check.
- Added the "Spatial data quality" and "Attribute data quality" tabs. Checks
  are divided between them by meaning, and the tabs become available after
  the first scan.
- Added "Select all", "Clear all" and "Defaults" buttons above the check list of
  both quality tabs; the check list now scrolls.
- Added a results table under the check list: rows are files, columns are the
  statistics of each selected check. The "Run selected checks" button moved
  above the table, and a single "Export" button below the table offers Excel
  and HTML.
- Added a "Control and invisible characters" attribute check:
  tabs, line feeds, carriage returns, NUL/ESC, no-break and zero-width spaces,
  soft hyphens, line/paragraph separators and the BOM in text values, with
  character names, feature counts and escaped examples in the report.
- Added an "Attribute duplicates (very slow!)" check: full row
  duplicates, composite key duplicates over text fields, matches ignoring case
  and extra spaces, and partial occurrences with an occurrence percent.
- Results table cells now store the issue list: double-clicking a cell opens a
  detailed dialog with every finding.
- Added a "Blank strings" attribute check: text fields whose value is empty or
  consists only of spaces, reported with per-field counts and shares because
  such values are invisible to IS NULL and split sorting and grouping into a
  separate group.
- Added a "Leading and trailing spaces" check: values with leading or trailing
  spaces, tabs and line breaks, reported per field with leading/trailing counts
  and a sample with visible space symbols.
- Added a "Double spaces inside values" check: two or more consecutive spaces
  inside a value, usually produced by manual input or field concatenation,
  reported with per-field counts, shares and a visible sample.
- Added a "Numbers stored as text" check: text fields whose values are integers
  or real numbers, reported with integer/real counts, shares and a sample,
  because such fields compare alphabetically and cannot be used in arithmetic.
- Added an "Abnormal text length" check: per text field the average value
  length and the standard deviation are computed and values longer than the
  average by more than three deviations are reported with the statistics,
  feature ids and a sample.
- Added a small "Add to current project" button to the Files tab: the selected
  files are loaded as layers into the open QGIS project, containers with all of
  their layers, already present sources are skipped.
- The feature count check is now "Refine feature count" only: it fills the
  "Features" column and no longer flags empty layers or files without features;
  those findings live on the attribute data tab.
- Added a "Dates outside a reasonable range" check: date, timestamp and text
  fields with years before 1900 or after the current year, including the zero
  date, reported with year bounds, feature ids and values.
- Added a "Suspicious field names" check: empty names,
  NULL/None/NaN names, digit-only names and technical import names such as
  Field1, Column3 or Unnamed: 0, reported per field with the reason.

