Version 1.38.0 — 2026-11-18
Previous GitHub release: v1.36.0 (2026-11-16)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.38.0 adds an "Attribute completeness check" and a "Topology
check".

Changes in 1.38.0
-----------------
- Added the "Attribute completeness check":
  - NULL, empty strings and whitespace-only strings are treated as
    empty values;
  - a fill rate is calculated for every field and for the layer as a
    whole, together with the share of completely empty features;
  - fields with a NOT NULL constraint and primary key fields are
    considered required, and empty values in them are reported
    separately;
  - optional fields below 50% fill are reported;
  - a layer is considered almost empty when less than 5% of cells are
    filled or at least 95% of features have no filled attributes;
  - a per-layer summary is shown in the "Issues" tooltip, and the
    report includes the fill rate of every field in problematic
    layers.
- Added the "Topology check":
  - polygon overlaps are detected pairwise by intersection area;
  - enclosed gaps are found in the layer union; a gap is reported when
    its boundary touches two or more features, so an interior hole of a
    single polygon is not treated as a gap;
  - line endpoints are dangling when they neither coincide with
    another line endpoint nor lie on another line;
  - interior line intersections and line overlaps are reported
    separately; shared endpoints and T-junctions are valid
    connections;
  - invalid and empty geometries are skipped because the geometry
    validity check covers them;
  - up to 1,000 detailed issues are stored per layer.
- Both checks are optional and disabled by default.
- Russian and English interface strings, README, metadata and tests
  were updated.

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.38.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

