Version 1.37.0 — 2026-11-17
Previous GitHub release: v1.36.0 (2026-11-16)

Overview
--------
ZGeo 1.37.0 adds a "GeoJSON check": coordinates, ring closure,
bbox and Feature/GeometryCollection structure.

Changes in 1.37.0
-----------------
- Added the "GeoJSON check":
  - coordinates must be finite numbers and positions must contain at
    least two numbers;
  - longitude is checked against [-180, 180] and latitude against
    [-90, 90], and signs of swapped latitude/longitude are reported;
  - rings must contain at least four positions and be closed (the
    first and last positions must match);
  - LineString and MultiLineString geometries must contain at least
    two positions;
  - optional bbox values are checked for a length of 4 or 6 numbers,
    finite values and minimum/maximum order;
  - Feature, FeatureCollection and GeometryCollection structure and
    required fields are validated, including nested geometry
    collections;
  - up to 1,000 detailed issues are stored per file; a summary with
    counts by category is shown in the "Issues" tooltip.
- The check is optional, disabled by default and appears in the
  Checks window only when .json or .geojson files are found.
- Russian and English interface strings, README, metadata and tests
  were updated.

Compatibility
-------------
- QGIS 3.16 and newer, including QGIS 4 / Qt 6.
- Python 3.9+.
- Windows is the primary target; the plugin uses QGIS and PyQt APIs.

Installation
------------
1. Download `zgeo-1.37.0.zip`.
2. In QGIS open Plugins → Manage and Install Plugins → Install from ZIP.
3. Select the downloaded archive and restart QGIS if it was running.

